---
import BaseLayout from "../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArrowIcon from "../site/components/ArrowIcon.astro";
import { siteDetails } from "../site/data/site";
import "../site/styles/about.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Why local — Mourne Made" description="Mourne Made is a Dundrum and Newcastle studio that shows local businesses what their website could become — then puts paid work back into the community.">
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--list about-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why local</p>
      <h1>The street should look as good online as it feels in person.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Mourne Made starts close to home: independent owners first, then the clubs, charities and public services that hold local life together.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="founder-note" aria-labelledby="founder-heading">
    <div class="shell founder-note-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who you are dealing with</p>
        <h2 id="founder-heading">I’m {siteDetails.founderFirstName}, from Dundrum.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="founder-note-copy">
        <p>Mourne Made is run by me, {siteDetails.founder}. I make each concept and keep the first conversation direct, so you will not be passed into a sales team.</p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href={siteDetails.emailHref}>Email {siteDetails.email}</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="principle-row"><span class="principle-number">01</span><h3>See the change first</h3><p>You get a free before-and-after concept before any decision. It makes the difference concrete and keeps the next step low-risk.</p></div>
      <div class="principle-row"><span class="principle-number">02</span><h3>Show the place people already know</h3><p>Locals know the welcome, the produce, the craft. Online should carry the same impression — and where it falls short, a concept makes the gap easy to see.</p></div>
      <div class="principle-row"><span class="principle-number">03</span><h3>Benefit stays nearby</h3><p>Paid projects keep the studio running. A share of that capacity goes back into free or reduced-cost help for clubs, charities and organisations with a clear need.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="studio-faq" aria-labelledby="studio-faq-heading">
    <div class="shell studio-faq-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Straight answers</p>
        <h2 id="studio-faq-heading">Before you ask.</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="studio-faq-list">
        <div>
          <dt>Is the concept really free?</dt>
          <dd>Yes. The focused before-and-after is free and there is no obligation to continue. It is useful on its own, not a redesign held back for a sales call.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>What would paid work cost?</dt>
          <dd>You receive a fixed written quote before paid work begins. The job can stay small — one useful page or improvement first — and nothing starts until you accept the scope and price.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Are hosting and domain costs hidden?</dt>
          <dd>No. A quote separates the build, domain and hosting. You can keep a suitable provider you already use; there is no forced long-term subscription.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>How long does it take?</dt>
          <dd>I confirm the concept delivery date when I reply. If you choose to continue, the paid schedule and its checkpoints are agreed before work starts.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="community">
    <div class="shell community-grid">
      <article class="community-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">For businesses</p>
        <h2>Ready to grow online</h2>
        <p>Focused websites, richer menus and recipes, better galleries, clearer booking paths and stronger local discovery.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="community-card community-card-community">
        <p class="eyebrow">For the community</p>
        <h2>Useful work when the budget is tight</h2>
        <p>Selected clubs, charities and community projects can receive reduced-cost or contributed work as capacity allows.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="shell button-row">
      <a class="button button-blue" href="/request/">Request a free before-and-after <ArrowIcon /></a>
      <a class="text-link" href={siteDetails.emailHref}>Or email {siteDetails.founderFirstName} directly</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
